ot for TV. This isn't like adapting Dickens, who wrote perfect, straightforward, linear narratives. Galsworthy is more complicated than that. So we had to look at the back story and tease out the important things and put them on ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Forsyte_Saga_(2002_TV_series)\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"d5249f440c723fdaf34038a301ede0715f82a2d52c092db4491f70b4c93c1f08\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"f8e9d6222946e27ab3fc4f121f9f76e0082a9665037c377b048fb370970971d3\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"TV show character four marriages one surviving child\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d119\"},\"ref\":\"d119\",\"snippet\":\" ... Every woman who gets involved with Nate Romanowski - the series' resident badass - meets an untimely end.\\n\\n- The Cat Who... Series: Supporting character Iris Cobb was married three times, and all three of her husbands predeceased her — her first one (and the father of her only son) died of ... \",\"title\":\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/CartwrightCurse\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d107\"},\"ref\":\"d107\",\"snippet\":\" ... With Procter & Gamble unable to make room for the new series in its line up, she put All My Children on hold. Nixon became head writer of Another World where she used the model of the Erica character to create a brand new character: Rachel Davis. Nixon said ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erica_Kane\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_recei